**Butanone.** There are three hydrogen environments (butanal would have four):

- singlet near 2.1 ppm: $\text{CH}_3$ next to C=O (3H);
- quartet near 2.45 ppm: $\text{CH}_2$ next to a $\text{CH}_3$ (2H);
- triplet near 1.05 ppm: $\text{CH}_3$ next to a $\text{CH}_2$ (3H).

There is no aldehyde proton near 9–10 ppm.
